   "source": [
    "# MovieLens ml-latest-small - Exploratory Data Analysis (CF Focus)\n",
    "\n",
    "## Dataset Overview\n",
    "- **Movies**: 9,742\n",
    "- **Ratings**: 100,836 (from 610 users)\n",
    "- **Tags**: 3,683\n",
    "- **Links**: TMDB/IMDB IDs for 9,742 movies\n",
    "\n",
    "## CF-Specific Analysis Goals\n",
    "1. **Sparsity** - User-item matrix density\n",
    "2. **Rating distributions** - Per user / per movie\n",
    "3. **Cold start analysis** - Users/movies with few ratings\n",
    "4. **Train/test split strategy** - User-based vs time-based"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "sys.path.append('..')\n",
    "\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "from src.data_loader import load_raw_data\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.set_style('whitegrid')\n",
    "pd.set_option('display.max_columns', None)\n",
    "pd.set_option('display.width', 200)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "data = load_raw_data()\n",
    "movies = data['movies']\n",
    "ratings = data['ratings']\n",
    "links = data['links']\n",
    "tags = data['tags']\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Movies shape:', movies.shape)\n",
    "print('Ratings shape:', ratings.shape)\n",
    "print('Links shape:', links.shape)\n",
    "print('Tags shape:', tags.shape)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "movies.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ratings.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ratings['rating'].describe()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Rating distribution\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 4))\n",
    "ratings['rating'].hist(bins=10, edgecolor='black')\n",
    "plt.title('Rating Distribution (1-5 scale)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Rating')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Count')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Ratings per user - critical for CF\n",
    "user_rating_counts = ratings.groupby('userId').size()\n",
    "print('Ratings per user:')\n",
    "print(user_rating_counts.describe())\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 4))\n",
    "plt.subplot(1, 2, 1)\n",
    "user_rating_counts.hist(bins=50, edgecolor='black')\n",
    "plt.title('Number of Ratings per User')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Ratings Count')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Number of Users')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.subplot(1, 2, 2)\n",
    "sns.boxplot(x=user_rating_counts)\n",
    "plt.title('Ratings per User - Boxplot')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Ratings per movie - critical for CF\n",
    "movie_rating_counts = ratings.groupby('movieId').size()\n",
    "print('Ratings per movie:')\n",
    "print(movie_rating_counts.describe())\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 4))\n",
    "plt.subplot(1, 2, 1)\n",
    "movie_rating_counts.hist(bins=50, edgecolor='black')\n",
    "plt.title('Number of Ratings per Movie')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Ratings Count')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Number of Movies')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.subplot(1, 2, 2)\n",
    "sns.boxplot(x=movie_rating_counts)\n",
    "plt.title('Ratings per Movie - Boxplot')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Sparsity analysis\n",
    "n_users = ratings['userId'].nunique()\n",
    "n_movies = ratings['movieId'].nunique()\n",
    "total_possible = n_users * n_movies\n",
    "observed = len(ratings)\n",
    "sparsity = 1 - (observed / total_possible)\n",
    "\n",
    f'Users: {n_users:,}'\n",
    f'Movies: {n_movies:,}'\n",
    f'Total possible ratings: {total_possible:,}'\n",
    f'Observed ratings: {observed:,}'\n",
    f'Sparsity: {sparsity:.4%}'\n",
    f'Density: {(1-sparsity):.4%}'"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Cold start analysis\n",
    "# Users with very few ratings\n",
    "low_activity_users = user_rating_counts[user_rating_counts < 5]\n",
    f'Users with <5 ratings: {len(low_activity_users)} ({len(low_activity_users)/n_users:.1%})'\n",
    "\n",
    "# Movies with very few ratings\n",
    "low_activity_movies = movie_rating_counts[movie_rating_counts < 5]\n",
    f'Movies with <5 ratings: {len(low_activity_movies)} ({len(low_activity_movies)/n_movies:.1%})'\n",
    "\n",
    "# Movies with NO ratings\n",
    "rated_movie_ids = set(ratings['movieId'].unique())\n",
    "all_movie_ids = set(movies['movieId'].unique())\n",
    "unrated_movies = all_movie_ids - rated_movie_ids\n",
    f'Movies with 0 ratings: {len(unrated_movies)} ({len(unrated_movies)/n_movies:.1%})'"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Genres analysis (for potential hybrid later)\n",
    "movies['genres_list'] = movies['genres'].str.split('|')\n",
    "all_genres = [g for sublist in movies['genres_list'] for g in sublist]\n",
    "from collections import Counter\n",
    "genre_counts = Counter(all_genres)\n",
    "genre_df = pd.DataFrame(genre_counts.items(), columns=['genre', 'count']).sort_values('count', ascending=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\n",
    "sns.barplot(data=genre_df.head(20), x='count', y='genre')\n",
    "plt.title('Top 20 Genres by Movie Count')\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "genre_df.head(20)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Temporal analysis - for time-based splits\n",
    "ratings['timestamp'] = pd.to_datetime(ratings['timestamp'], unit='s')\n",
    "print('Date range:', ratings['timestamp'].min(), 'to', ratings['timestamp'].max())\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 4))\n",
    "ratings['timestamp'].dt.year.value_counts().sort_index().plot(kind='bar')\n",
    "plt.title('Ratings per Year')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Year')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Count')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# User rating patterns\n",
    "user_avg_rating = ratings.groupby('userId')['rating'].mean()\n",
    "user_std_rating = ratings.groupby('userId')['rating'].std()\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 4))\n",
    "plt.subplot(1, 2, 1)\n",
    "user_avg_rating.hist(bins=30, edgecolor='black')\n",
    "plt.title('Average Rating per User')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Avg Rating')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Number of Users')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.subplot(1, 2, 2)\n",
    "user_std_rating.hist(bins=30, edgecolor='black')\n",
    "plt.title('Rating Std Dev per User')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Std Dev')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Number of Users')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Key Findings for CF Design\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **High sparsity** (~97%) - SVD handles well; k-NN needs shrinkage\n",
    "2. **Power-law distributions** - Few users/movies have many ratings\n",
    "3. **Cold start significant** - ~X% users, ~Y% movies have <5 ratings\n",
    "4. **Temporal span** - Ratings from YYYY to YYYY, enables time-based split\n",
    "5. **Rating scale 1-5** - Explicit feedback, good for SVD regression\n",
    "\n",
    "## Next Steps (Day 2-3)\n",
    "1. Build `src/preprocessing.py` - clean, filter, create user-item matrix\n",
    "2. Filter: movies with ≥5 ratings, users with ≥5 ratings\n",
    "3. Create surprise `Dataset` with `Reader(rating_scale=(1, 5))`\n",
    "4. Train/test split: **user-based** (hold out last N ratings per user) or **time-based**\n",
    "5. Save processed data for model training"
   ]
  }
